00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:24,000
I observed some helicopter scouters this weekend and I thought I'd share.

24
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:29,000
There was another large troop camping next to us and they had an awful lot of parents with them.

25
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Their camp kitchen was in close proximity to us and I watched them over the weekend.

26
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:40,000
I never saw a single scout enter the kitchen to light a stove or heat some water or clean a dish.

27
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:43,000
The parents and the Scoutmaster did everything.

28
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Our boys kind of hunkered down over their backpack stoves and heated cup of noodles or toasted, a pop tart.

29
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,000
It's the same everywhere, isn't it?

30
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:55,000
That's the same menu: cup of noodles and pop tarts.

31
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:00,000
